{"results": [{"id": "FAM:SF-APPM-022", "score": 0.154, "document": "# FAM:SF-APPM-022 | Study family SF-APPM-022: Superstar suppression profiles (incl. Q5c sequential triggering)\n- observed_research_question: Superstar suppression profiles (incl. Q5c sequential triggering)\n- auto_outcome_status: inconclusive\n- observed_hypothesis: Specific opposing lineups, defenders, play types and preceding opponent play types suppress star efficiency.\n- observed_result: Q5c verdict 'rank-1 suppressor varies meaningfully across players'; e.g. Jokic after opp POST_UP 1.1271 (-0.0675, SE +/-0.0500, n=480); Curry forced POST_UP -0.209.\n- auto_failure_mechanism: E_unclear (mechanism unclear from the records)\n- observed_failure_evidence: Rank-1 deltas mostly within 1-2 SE with no multiple-comparison control; OTHER artifact flagged in doc.\n- observed_sample_and_power: SE per cell reported\n- auto_validation_status: no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED\n- observed_method: Initiator possessions for 4 then ~30 stars (gate >=15); Q5c ranks opponent prior-PT by target PPP for 14 players; reruns 2026-05-06 and 2026-05-30."}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPM-058", "score": 0.11, "document": "# FAM:SF-APPM-058 | Study family SF-APPM-058: PNR shot-level season rates vs possession labels\n- observed_research_question: PNR shot-level season rates vs possession labels\n- auto_outcome_status: not a hypothesis test\n- observed_hypothesis: PBP-derived shot-level PNR rates sit in a realistic band (script notes possession-level rates will be higher) and vary by team as expected.\n- observed_result: 2024-25 shot-level PNR share of half-court shots ranges from OKC 7.567% (498/6581) and BOS 7.854% to IND 13.824% (856/6192) and NYK 11.959%. ATL 11.361%, DEN 11.404%, PHX 10.232% (bh 7.050 / roll 3.181).\n- auto_failure_mechanism: E_unclear (mechanism unclear from the records)\n- observed_failure_evidence: No pass/fail gate in the output; rates are a calibration input for PBPProxyPNR (later logs show calibrated PNR ~17.9-19.6% of possessions).\n- observed_sample_and_power: 30 teams, half_court_shots ~5994-6581\n- auto_validation_status: no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED\n- observed_verdict: descriptive\n- observed_failure_type: E_unclear"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-CHT-009", "score": 0.108, "document": "# FAM:SF-CHT-009 | Study family SF-CHT-009: Superstar suppression by lineup and forced play type\n- observed_research_question: Superstar suppression by lineup and forced play type\n- auto_outcome_status: not a hypothesis test\n- observed_hypothesis: Named star initiators have identifiable lineup and forced-play-type suppressors in the possession graph.\n- observed_result: Jokic vs MIN lineup PPP 0.814, -0.385 (n=59); Curry vs HOU 0.851, -0.358 (n=47); Doncic vs LAC 0.733, -0.396 (n=30); Giannis forced PULL_UP 0.848, -0.540 vs preferred DRIVE (largest gap).\n- auto_failure_mechanism: E_unclear (mechanism unclear from the records)\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:PLACEBO_DEPENDENCE\n- observed_failure_evidence: No placebo or matching; later sequence work treated similar star-chain gaps as artifacts.\n- observed_sample_and_power: n>=30 for lineup cells cited\n- auto_validation_status: no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED\n- observed_method: Jokic/Curry/Doncic/Giannis; min-15 gate on 8 play types; opposing DEFENSE_LINEUP ~84% coverage; 272-row CSV."}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-012", "score": 0.1, "document": "# FAM:SF-APPS-012 | Study family SF-APPS-012: Defensive PPP allowed and possession share, RS vs playoffs\n- observed_research_question: Defensive PPP allowed and possession share, RS vs playoffs\n- auto_outcome_status: not a hypothesis test\n- observed_hypothesis: Playoff defenses suppress DRIVE more than RS defenses (both lower PPP allowed and lower share).\n- observed_result: DRIVE allowed 1.191 -> 0.923 (-0.268), share 21.2% -> 18.2%; PNR -0.139, share +12.1pp; PULL_UP +0.341, share -7.6pp.\n- auto_failure_mechanism: E_unclear (mechanism unclear from the records)\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:LABEL_ERROR\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:MECHANICAL_FLOOR\n- observed_failure_evidence: No inferential test; PNR share jump of +12.1pp may reflect tagging differences.\n- observed_sample_and_power: 25 teams\n- auto_validation_status: no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED\n- observed_method: 25 defensive teams, min 30 poss per cell; RS vs playoff PPP allowed and opponent possession share by PT.\n- observed_verdict: descriptive\n- observed_failure_type: E_unclear"}], "n_results": 4}

Stage 2. Using the retrieval result above (follow-up tools are allowed within the tool budget), complete steps 4 to 9
and reply with the final action. Output schema (all fields required):
